Handling Missing Values
Check missing Price values  
Formula:

Code
=COUNTIF(C2:C100,"")
→ Counts blank cells in the Price column.

Strategy for missing Price

Impute with average:

Code
=IF(C2="",AVERAGE($C$2:$C$100),C2)
Or remove rows if price is critical.

Missing Category values

Impute with most frequent category or assign "Miscellaneous":

Code
=IF(B2="", "Miscellaneous", B2)
2. 🔵 Correcting Inconsistent Data
Product Name text formats  
Standardize case:

Code
=PROPER(D2)
Category typos  
Use Find & Replace (Ctrl+H):

Replace “Electroncs” → “Electronics”

Replace “Furnture” → “Furniture”

Standardization: Apply across the column to unify spelling and format.

3. 🟢 Removing Duplicates
Identify duplicates

Data tab → Remove Duplicates.

Formula check:

Code
=COUNTIFS(A:A,A2,B:B,B2,C:C,C2)>1
→ Returns TRUE if row is duplicate.

4. 🟣 Splitting and Merging Data
Split Product ID (e.g., 20210101-IN):

Manufacturing Date:

Code
=LEFT(A2,8)
Country Code:

Code
=RIGHT(A2,2)
Merge Brand + Product Name into “Product Brand”:

Code
=B2 & " " & C2
5. 🔴 Number Formatting
Price column → Currency format

Select column → Format Cells → Currency.

Shortcut: Ctrl+Shift+$.

Manufacturing Date → DD-MM-YYYY format

Format Cells → Date → Custom → DD-MM-YYYY.

6. 🟤 Conditional Formatting
Data Bars in Price column

Home → Conditional Formatting → Data Bars → Gradient Fill.

Highlight Electronics in Category column

New Rule → Use formula:

Code
=$B2="Electronics"
Apply fill color (e.g., yellow).